# The bin entry is executed through its shebang on macOS and Linux. A CRLF
# checkout turns "#!/usr/bin/env node" into "#!/usr/bin/env node", and the
# kernel then looks for an interpreter literally named "node". The package
# is authored on Windows, so without this the failure is one careless copy
# away and it never shows up on the machine that made it.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
